   how_label:"How it works",
   hero_overview_detail:"Your whole drive shelf at a glance: every cataloged drive, how full it is, what's at risk and what's reclaimable. Start here, then dive into Search, the Storage Map, projects or duplicates.",
   hero_drives_detail:"All your drives in one place — model, capacity, usage and contents. Add a drive by scanning it once; from then on it's searchable forever, even back in the drawer.",
   hero_map_detail:"An interactive sunburst of one drive: the biggest folders and files, sized by the space they take. Click a wedge to zoom in, the center to go back. Find space hogs in seconds — even while the drive is unplugged, because Disky reads from the catalog, not the disk.",
   hero_dupes_detail:"Disky compares files by <b>checksum</b> (their actual content), not by name — renamed or nested copies still match. Each card is a folder whose content provably exists on <b>multiple drives</b>. Opening it shows three honest numbers per drive: the <b>entire</b> folder there, the <b>identical</b> share, and what exists <b>only there</b>. You choose which copy stays — released is only what provably (checksum + size) also lives on the keeper; everything else stays untouched. Nothing is deleted until you confirm; everything goes to the Trash (recoverable).",
   hero_search_detail:"Search file or folder names, including small typos. Results show the drive and cataloged path. Offline, you can view the catalog location; connect the drive to open it in Finder. Refresh the catalog after renaming or moving files.",
   hero_gather_detail:"Collect projects from across your drives into one list, then copy them all to one destination in a single pass — only the drives you need plugged in. Disky reads only; your originals aren't moved until you confirm.",
